    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30289" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Myrtōus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μυρτῶος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Myrtoan</i>: Myrtoum
			mare, <i>the Myrtoan Sea, a part of the Ægean
				Sea, between Crete, the Peloponnesus, and Eubœa, which
				derives its name from the island of</i> Myrtos, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11,
				18, § 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				1, 14</span></i>: so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pelagus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 3, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 7, 10</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					372</span></i>
			.</div>
